**Aim:** To find the Kth smallest element using the Median of Medians algorithm.

**Pseudocode:**

1. Start.
2. Read array A and K.
3. If the array contains at most five elements, sort it and return the Kth element.
4. Divide the array into groups of five elements.
5. Sort each group and find its median.
6. Find the median of all group medians.
7. Select the median as the pivot.
8. Divide the array into smaller, equal, and greater elements.
9. If K is in the smaller part, recursively search the smaller part.
10. If K is in the equal part, return the pivot.
11. Otherwise, search the greater part with adjusted K.
12. Display the Kth smallest element.
13. Stop.

**Time Complexity:** O(n)

**Space Complexity:** O(n)
